    "guidance": "**Preferred default among this set, but not fail-safe: 8/12 final passes (66.7%) in distribution.** Use from retrieval overlap when fingers are closed and the peg-to-TCP transform is stable over both causal frames. The held-peg anchor is intended for a jointly displaced but still rigidly held peg/TCP pair; that displacement case has no OOD validation. Avoid dropped/slipping pegs, unreliable peg pose, lost wall/lid clearance, or routes made unreachable by displacement. If substantial destination/fixture motion is the concern, the documents prefer the hole-frame policy, again without OOD evidence. The validation failure signature is strong: all four final failures accumulated 78–101 IK-unconverged steps, whereas all eight passes had zero; three failures also ended with the cover collapsed near 0 rad, and every failure lacked final axis alignment/insertion. Abort or switch on repeated poor IK diagnostics, limit contact, cover collapse, peg/TCP drift, or hole-relative error that stops shrinking. All eight passes ended aligned, inserted, cover-open, and at task success, but all runs also showed a transient pass before final scoring; do not assume a reached stage will persist. Hand off in the supervised outgoing overlap to `align_and_insert_peg` once coupling is stable and the peg is aligned, laterally centered, and descending; if insertion/task success is already verified, terminate rather than invoke a successor. Preserve causal history and refresh the peg anchor every eight executed actions."
